   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, reviewer of #1287): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 2383a78\n\n1. **Medium (LESSONS 2, harness L01)**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Composer/ComposerCardGrowthTests.swift:74-85`. The tests do not fail without the fix. The fix is one line in the view, `ReplyComposerView.swift:204` (`measured.editorHeight` → `layoutWithChips.editorHeight`). Put that line back and both new tests stay green. They only check `withChips` and the way `textCap` subtracts `chips`, and `textCap` already did that before this PR. `noChipsLeavesTheLayoutUnchanged` passes trivially: `layout(lines: 12)` already has `chips == 0`.\n   **Fix:** add a hosted test in `ComposerLayoutHostedTests`: insert a chip with `model.imageChips.append(...)`, write `longText`, then check two things. The editor frame's height must equal the layout's `editorHeight` with the chips row. The card must not exceed the room. Show it red with line 204 reverted.\n2. **Low**, `ReplyComposerView.swift:154`. The probe gets `measured`, whose `chips` is always 0. It does not get the layout the view now draws from. Because of this, a hosted test cannot see #1286. Today it would check `editor.height` against a cap without the chips row, which is the old bug.\n   **Fix:** send `layoutWithChips` to the probe (`.onChange(of: layoutWithChips, initial: true)`). This is needed for finding 1.\n\n**Checked, nothing found:** arithmetic (top 70, controls 56, line 20, available 600: without chips `textCap` 450, `editorHeight` 466, `cardHeight` 600; with chips 60: 390, 406, 600; difference 60); chips not counted twice; no name clash; `ReplyComposerView.swift` still 398 lines; `swiftlint` clean on the 3 files. Not built or run (Linux).\n\nRound 1 of 3.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
