   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, round 3): APPROVE** — head 71022bed1411d7b0afd63e98391cc9420c1431c6\n\n1. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Composer/ComposerLayoutHostedTests.swift:118-122`: the test does not show that it can tell the fixed code from the broken one. The editor's cap is `max(6 lines, room − top − chips − controls − 24)`. On a device where the room left over is already under six lines, the cap is the same with or without chips. If the editor reverted to reading `measured.editorHeight`, the test would then stay green. On the iPhone 18 Pro with a 336 pt keyboard there is about 180–230 pt of room, so the two cases differ by 50–66 pt and the test does go red. Fix: add `#expect(layout.withChips(height: 0).editorHeight - layout.editorHeight > 1, \"the chips row changes the cap\")`.\n2. **Low**, `ComposerLayoutHostedTests.swift:57-63` together with `ComposerScreen.swift:17-23`: `keyboardHeight` converts the frame through `isKeyWindow` and has no fallback. The test window is only unhidden, never made key, so the conversion uses the host app's key window. If there is no key window, or the notification arrives before `onReceive` subscribes, `availableHeight` stays nil and the `#require` fails. That is a possible red failure, never a false green. Fix if it ever turns flaky: call `window.makeKeyAndVisible()` when `keyboard != nil`.\n\nChecks against the round-2 findings: `try #require(Bool, \"…\")` compiles; `guard isPhone` correct; `abs(card.height − textCardHeight) < 1` checks the drawn card; undoing each part of the fix turns the test red (editor alone: editor and card checks fail; probe alone and all of it: the `chips == 66` check fails); the chips row is drawn at exactly 66 pt. Hand arithmetic of `ComposerCardGrowthTests` matches (600, 60 pt). `swiftlint` clean on the 4 files. Not built or run (Linux).\n\nRound 3 of 3. The two Low items are not applied, to keep the approved head; the author notes them for a flaky-test follow-up if the hosted test ever turns red.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
